def _oc_deployment_doctrine_lines(summary: Dict[str, Any], meta: Dict[str, Any]) -> List[str]:
    manager = meta.get("manager_payload") if isinstance(meta.get("manager_payload"), dict) else {}
    enterprise = meta.get("enterprise_payload") if isinstance(meta.get("enterprise_payload"), dict) else {}
    direct = enterprise.get("direct_muscle", {}) if isinstance(enterprise, dict) else {}
    plants = direct.get("plants", []) if isinstance(direct, dict) else []
    manager_n = manager.get("scenario_count", "not executed") if manager else "not executed"
    return [
        "Omni-Compass is designed as a deployable governing core rather than a single fixed integration pattern. The same Piece I state-and-feedback mechanism can be connected above existing managers, between managers and actuators, or directly to operational muscles through domain-specific safety and command adapters.",
        "Manager-coexistence mode receives telemetry and proposals from orchestration, observability, infrastructure, scheduling, policy, and incident-management systems, then returns a coordinated governing directive. Representative interfaces include Kubernetes, Terraform, Datadog, Grafana, GitOps controllers, Slurm-class schedulers, service meshes, alerting systems, and related managers.",
        "Hybrid mode preserves selected managers while allowing direct command paths to lower-level controls and muscles, including PID controllers, model-predictive controllers, Kalman estimators, Adam optimizers, robotic joints, motors, thermal plants, networks, power systems, aerospace actuators, and other bounded operational interfaces.",
        "Direct-to-muscle mode bypasses selected supervisory managers and applies the Omni-Compass governing state through verified actuator adapters. Replacement or consolidation of manager functions is a deployment objective that requires environment-specific interface mapping, safety interlocks, fallback behavior, load testing, and acceptance evidence before production removal of incumbent software.",
        f"Executed evidence in this package includes {summary.get('total', 0)} canonical governing trajectories, {manager_n} matched fragmented-stack scenarios, and direct-muscle plant evaluations across {len(plants) if isinstance(plants, list) else 'multiple'} declared plant families when the enterprise suite is present. Those results demonstrate implemented deployment surfaces and comparative synthetic plant behavior; they do not claim universal controller superiority, production safety, or that every vendor product or physical plant was reproduced in full.",
        "The governing distinction is architectural: Omni-Compass may govern managers, govern muscles through managers, govern managers and muscles together, or govern muscles directly. The selected deployment level is an engineering choice; the canonical mathematical core remains the same while adapters, constraints, permissions, and safety contracts change by domain.",
        f"The law is stack-count agnostic at the mathematical level: local weakness, excess, conflict, or drift is represented through the common state and returned as a bounded coordinated directive. Operational scale is nevertheless constrained by telemetry throughput, state aggregation, adapter fan-in, latency, partitioning, redundancy, and compute capacity. Million-stack operation is an owner scalability objective requiring distributed implementation and scale certification; it is not represented as measured by the present {summary.get('total', 0)}-run canonical campaign.",
        "The intended governing effect is system-wide coherence redistribution: under-responsive modules receive increased corrective authority, over-responsive modules are damped or rebalanced, and conflicting manager or muscle proposals are reconciled against the same admissibility and basin-retention contract.",
    ]


