        "AUTOPILOT MODE authorizes the bounded governing directive within the declared permissions, command limits, admissibility rules, and safety envelope. MANUAL / SUPERVISED MODE computes the same directive but reserves release authority to an authenticated operator or external approval gate. OBSERVE-ONLY MODE permits shadow evaluation and evidence collection without production command authority. OFF MODE prevents the governing execution from starting.",
        "The kill switch is a fail-safe authority control, not a substitute for cyber security. Production deployment requires identity and access management, signed builds, least-privilege adapters, network segmentation, audit logging, rollback, fallback control, command-rate limits, and independent safety interlocks so compromise of the supervisory plane cannot silently become unrestricted actuator authority.",
